   "fp_waiver_note": "It's possible (but not likely) that Emari Demercado will be the Texans' lead RB when they host the Colts this week. Woody Marks left the Texans' Week 10 loss to the Browns with a concussion. David Montgomery has missed the last four games with a groin injury, although he returned to practice last week. Demercado played 22 snaps in Week 10 and had 7-16-0 rushing and one catch for -1 yard. It seems as if Montgomery will be back this week. He practiced in full last Friday, but the Texans chose not to activate him for their Week 10 game against the Browns. Marks has little chance to clear concussion protocol before the Texans' Thursday-night game. If Demercado has a significant role in Week 11, he could be playable in an ultra-favorable matchup against the Colts, who went into Week 10 with a run defense that ranked 31st in DVOA and 32nd in EPA per rush."
