   "position": "TE",
   "nfl_team": "LV",
   "proj": 7.11,
   "ros_rank": 123.0,
   "fp_waiver_rank": 9.0,
   "injury": "ACTIVE",
   "replaces": "Greg Dulcich",
   "ros_rank_gain": 19.0,
   "week_proj_gain": -3.18,
   "priority": "MEDIUM",
   "availability": "ESPN_WAIVERS",
   "espn_pct_owned": 18.4,
   "fp_waiver_note": "With Brock Bowers dealing with an ankle injury that could potentially cost him one or more games, and with the Raiders devoid of impactful wide receivers, TE Michael Mayer's short-term target outlook has brightened. Mayer has 41-404-1 on 49 targets. Mayer has more receptions this season than any of the Las Vegas wideouts. This week, Mayer has a matchup against a Denver defense that has been a TE funnel. The Broncos have allowed the third-fewest fantasy points per game to wide receivers, but they've allowed the fourth-most fantasy points per game to tight ends. Rookie QB Fernando Mendoza might lean heavily on Mayer this week."
  },
  {
   "name": "Mike Gesicki",
   "position": "TE",
   "nfl_team": "CIN",
   "proj": 7.43,
   "ros_rank": 118.0,
   "fp_waiver_rank": 10.0,
   "injury": "ACTIVE",
   "replaces": "Greg Dulcich",
   "ros_rank_gain": 24.0,
   "week_proj_gain": -2.86,
   "priority": "MEDIUM",
   "availability": "ESPN_WAIVERS",
   "espn_pct_owned": 22.6,
   "fp_waiver_note": "Mike Gesicki doesn't offer a sturdy floor. He's had 11 or fewer receiving yards in four of his last five games. What Gesicki does offer is touchdown potential. He's caught six TD passes this season, and while Gesicki has gone two consecutive games without scoring a touchdown, he had a touchdown in five straight games from Week 3 to Week 8. Gesicki is attached to red-hot Bengals QB Joe Burrow, who's thrown 20 TD passes in his last five starts. This week, Burrow faces a Washington defense that has allowed the second-most fantasy points to tight ends. Giants TE Isaiah Likely torched the Commanders for 9-127-1 in Week 10."
  },
  {
   "name": "Seth McGowan",
   "position": "RB",
   "nfl_team": "IND",
   "proj": 5.28,
   "ros_rank": 137.0,
   "fp_waiver_rank": 15.0,
   "injury": "ACTIVE",
   "replaces": "Roschon Johnson",
   "ros_rank_gain": 113.0,
   "week_proj_gain": 5.28,
   "priority": "MEDIUM",
   "availability": "ESPN_WAIVERS",
   "espn_pct_owned": 10.8,
   "fp_waiver_note": "Well, well, well. It turns out Seth McGowan might have fantasy value after all, even though a Jonathan Taylor trade never came to fruition. We touted McGowan as a potential waiver pickup last week, since it seemed as if the Colts were destined to trade Taylor to one of the half-dozen or so teams rumored to be interested in his services. But there was no deal by last Tuesday's trade deadline, so interest in McGowan as a waiver claim fizzled. Against the Dolphins in Week 10, Taylor played 40 snaps, McGowan 17. But McGowan got carries on 12 of those 17 snaps and finished with 77 rushing yards and a touchdown. It's possible that going forward, the Colts use Taylor and McGowan in much the same way the Rams use Kyren Williams and Blake Corum. Williams typically plays a lot more snaps than Corum, but Corum has been getting either a carry or a target on more than half of his snaps. The Colts were run-heavy in their win over the Dolphins on Sunday, running the ball on 60.7% of their offensive snaps. The 3-7 Colts will not have the luxury of run-friendly game scripts very often, but they're likely to be fairly run-heavy anyway, since they're better at running the ball than throwing it, and since the Colts now have one of the worst WR collections in the league after trading away Keenan Allen and Josh Downs at the deadline. In a waiver week where there's very little of interest at the RB position, McGowan might be worth a bid if you need to patch a hole at the position."
  },
